cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Measuring Upstream Provenance at Cryptocurrency Mixer Entrances: A Cross-Actor Forensic Study"
message: "If you use this data or code, please cite the paper."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: "Xiao"
    given-names: "Yunlong"
  - family-names: "Lim"
    given-names: "Byunghwa"
abstract: >-
  Data and code for a forensic measurement of how far the upstream provenance
  before a cryptocurrency mixer deposit reaches across distinct laundering crews.
  Includes an evidence-gated dataset of 169 Tornado Cash entrance deposits, the
  reference feature-extraction code, the cross-crew evaluation, the temporally
  balanced background control (balanced_background/), and the figure scripts that
  regenerate Figures 3-7 and C1 from the archived data (Figures 1 and 2 are
  static overview graphics, verified by SHA-256).
keywords:
  - cryptocurrency mixer
  - anti-money-laundering forensics
  - upstream provenance
  - cross-actor generalization
  - missingness audit
license: 
  - MIT
  - CC-BY-4.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/0xXiaoyunlong/Measuring-upstream-provenance"
